  "Question": "Solve \\((x-2)²=3(x-2)\\). (Separate the two roots with a comma; be careful not to divide both sides by \\(x-2\\).)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2，5",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": true,
  "Solution": "Moving terms gives \\((x-2)²-3(x-2)=0\\). Factoring out the common factor gives \\((x-2)(x-2-3)=0\\), or \\((x-2)(x-5)=0\\), so \\(x=2\\) or \\(x=5\\). Dividing both sides by \\(x-2\\) would lose the root \\(x=2\\).",
